By default ext2 filesystems will have 5% reserved for use by the
superuser. I'm not even sure if other common filesystems used under
Linux (reiserfs, xfs, etc.) even _have_ reserved-blocks (FFS as used by
the BSDs also seems to be 5% by default). This is mainly so logs can
still be written, even if ordinary users fill up the filesystem.

